title text_grid -- per-cell foreground color, the colored terminal, GREEN
prompt Autonomous loop: continue taking agent-doable laps Lindy-first crux-first optimizing for the balance compass, deep-read one council-rota doc, send often, stop at custody gates.
think The prior lap's recommend named the nearer mechanical crux: teach text_grid a per-cell foreground so a header or a caret can carry its own color. A terminal surface shows colored text -- an author name, an unread badge, a caret -- so per-cell color is Lindy-durable floor every future glass surface (Grainphone, Realidream, Skate) stands on. It is also the one API move that unlocks color across the whole terminal-meets-pixels family.
think Accrete-never-break: rather than change render_grid/paint_grid (which would break scooter_paint and the selftest), I ADDED paint_grid_fg and render_grid_fg beside the single-ink verbs, untouched. The colored twin takes fg []color.Rgba of exactly cols*rows; cell (r,c) paints its glyph in fg[r*cols+c]. Placement is identical to paint_grid -- layout each row once, but paint each cell's one-glyph slice (scratch[c..c+1], already carrying pen_x=c*advance) in its own ink rather than the whole row in one. A mis-sized palette refuses GridFgMismatch by name before any pixel is allocated.
think Witness crux -- color is per cell, not shared, proven by measure: extended text_grid's own selftest so the existing witness covers it. A palette paints row 0 red and every other row black. Proved the colored face inks the SAME cells as the single-ink face (color moves ink, adds none -- changed count equals want_ink), then found the first fully-black inked pixel in row 0's band on the single-ink face and proved the colored face reads red (255,0,0) there -- so the ink is read per cell. The colored face round-trips through QOI byte-for-byte too, and a short palette refuses GridFgMismatch.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: the 16x3 selftest now also proves the per-cell palette. scooter_paint still GREEN (the single-ink verbs it calls are unchanged). tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, text_grid.rye plain 7-bit ASCII.
obs Balance lap held: a floor feature that serves the whole terminal family (color everywhere it shows text) rather than a new leaf; accretive so nothing already GREEN moved. The colored caret and colored author name a chat surface wants are now one call away.
obs Rota this lap (d27) deep-read item 20, context/QUIN.md -- the four faculties Kyri carries forward (Lattice's honest number, Scribble's open door, Lantern's marked proposed, Ember's earned craft) and Quin's two live hats. This rung is Lattice and Ember: color bound to a measured red pixel, the twin proven beside the elder before it is called done.
